# OPERATIONS §2.3 (M3) on a joint model (L §6.1): the member m is found from j's use line and matches its pin, so
# everything given loads: `ok`, then the joint model's own warnings load decides (own_spare and s read by nothing); the
# member's unread spare isn't the joint model's to warn (each member warns alone, L §8.5), as in run. Exit 0.
=== options check exit=0
=== j.tally
model j
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use m = "m/m.tally" sha256 "f76edd5d971df3215297a75df16c65e0210fbf0160b20fe11428c1c65ed4b933"

source s "s"

input y: int
input own_spare: int

ask q: y
=== m/m.tally
model mm
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input x: int
input spare: int

ask q: x
=== expect
ok
warning: WARN-UNREAD input own_spare is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD source s is read by nothing
